# Line-ending policy for Forever Guild Comms
#
# Store every text file as LF in the repository AND check it out as LF, so the
# working tree is identical on every machine regardless of each contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows clone with the common
# core.autocrlf=true converts the sources to CRLF on checkout, which git then
# reports as "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it".
#
# LF is already what the shipped sources use, and the WoW client's Lua
# interpreter reads either ending, so pinning LF changes nothing at runtime and
# removes the churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for the files that actually make up the addon, so the intent
# survives if the wildcard above is ever narrowed.
*.lua          text eol=lf
*.toc          text eol=lf
*.md           text eol=lf
LICENSE        text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
